. * FILTERS * (Please adapt according to your needs)
.  
. 
. keep if inlist(pop,1,2) /* Focus on pvt HH as other categories are unclear */
(89,279 observations deleted)

. keep if kidgeb04<0 /* Focus on relatively smaller families, as larger familie
> s might be distinct from smaller ones */
(38,389 observations deleted)

. drop if sex==2
(277,246 observations deleted)

. 
. * GENERATE VARIABLES * (Please adapt according to your needs)
. 
. g loginc = log(pglabgro+1) //Log of gross labour income
(111,459 missing values generated)

. 
. g daughter = kidsex01 == 2 | kidsex02 == 2 | kidsex03 == 2 // Indicator if an
> y of first three children are daughters 

. 
. g twindaughters = kidsex01 == 2 & kidsex02 == 2 & kidgeb01 == kidgeb02 // Fir
> st 2 kids twin daughters

. replace twindaughters = 1 if kidsex02 == 2 & kidsex03 == 2 & kidgeb02 == kidg
> eb03 // Kids 2 and 3 twin daughters
(473 real changes made)

. 
.         
. * HYPOTHESIS TEST FOR H2 * (Please adapt according to your needs)
. 
.         * Two-way fixed effects panel regression of time spent doing house wo
> rk on a dummy for whether have twin daughters. Fixed effects: Time (survey ye
> ar) & Region of birth. Controls: log of gross income, education (in years), a
> nd age. SEs clustered at region of birth. The estimation done only for male r
> espondents.
. 
. reghdfe pli0043_v3 twindaughters loginc pgbilzeit bioage if pli0043_v3>=0  & 
> pgbilzeit>0 & bioage>0, absorb(syear birthregion) cluster(birthregion)
(MWFE estimator converged in 5 iterations)

